comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T20:13:44.114Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1714 Greptile, fixed in this PR: the walk skipped recursion when an identity key held an object, so {audit_details: {author: {author: url}}} passed. The walk now recurses into every container, including one stored under an identity key; the case is in the spec.\n"
  "2026-11-12T21:00:55.740Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1714 Codex review (P2), fixed in this PR: the recursive walk judged every nested key named author, so a linked test whose assert_json_field_equals map checks an author field holding a public URL with an at sign in its path (an example.com profile URL) was refused at create. pm reads identities only at declared locations, so the walk now follows a declared table: the top-level author, assignee and claim_principal plus the entry paths comments/notes/learnings/dependencies/plan_decisions/plan_discoveries author and tests provenance author. A container stored at one of those locations is still identity data throughout (bounded at depth 4), so author holding an object with a nested URL credential stays refused. An author key in arbitrary field data, such as an assertion map or audit_details, is no longer judged. The refusal now names the entry path, for example comments[0].author.\n"
